# Golden vectors and conformance fixtures are CONTENT, not text: several suites
# byte-compare them against generator output or producer-recorded digests, and
# git's checkout EOL normalization on Windows rewrites LF to CRLF, failing those
# comparisons with byte-identical-looking diffs (third incident: agent-token
# vectors, adapter vendored fixtures, then PR #61's wire vectors). Marking the
# directories rather than waiting for each suite to adopt byte comparison and
# rediscover the trap. Parse-based consumers are unaffected either way.
clients/subc-client-swift/Tests/SubcClientTests/Fixtures/** -text
clients/subc-client-swift/Tests/SubcFedTests/Fixtures/** -text
docs/team-mode/fixtures/** -text
crates/agent-token-vectors/vectors/** -text
# Every crate's and client's golden and fixture directories, including ones
# added later: the fourth incident was a new crate (ck-bus) whose vendored
# foundation copy failed its sha256 check on Windows because its directory
# was not on the list above.
crates/*/tests/golden/** -text
crates/*/tests/fixtures/** -text
clients/*/tests/golden/** -text
vectors/app-open-v1/** -text
